<section class="story-hero">
 <div>
  <span class="story-kicker">Security and privacy</span>
  <h1>Built to be trusted with people&rsquo;s details</h1>
  <p class="lead">Care Core holds information about staff and about people who receive care. This is a plain summary of how it is protected, and where the responsibility passes to you.</p>
  <p class="story-note">The pictures are drawn illustrations with invented data.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="scene" aria-hidden="true"><div class="scene-bar"><span class="dot"></span>Change request: home address<span class="tag">Waiting for approval</span></div><div class="scene-body">
   <div class="diff"><div><small>Old</small>12 Harbour Road, Oban</div><div class="new"><small>New</small>4 Glen Street, Oban</div></div>
   <div class="srow"><div><div class="t">Asked by Alex Morgan</div><div class="s">Cannot approve their own request</div></div><span class="st gold">Waiting</span></div>
   <div class="srow"><div><div class="t">Line manager reviews</div><div class="s">Sees old and new side by side</div></div><span class="st thistle">Reviewing</span></div>
   <div class="srow"><div><div class="t">Recorded in the activity log</div><div class="s">Same transaction as the change</div></div><span class="st">Logged</span></div>
 </div><div class="scene-foot">Illustration with invented data</div></div>
</section>
<div class="sec-grid">
  <div class="sec-card"><span class="num">01</span><h2>Access by role</h2><p>Administrator, manager and staff roles are enforced on the server for every page and action. Care information is for managers and administrators only. One organisation can never see another&rsquo;s records.</p></div>
  <div class="sec-card"><span class="num">02</span><h2>Encrypted where it matters</h2><p>National Insurance and bank details are encrypted in the database (AES-256-GCM). Passwords are stored only as hashes; invitations and integration tokens only as hashes, shown once.</p></div>
  <div class="sec-card"><span class="num">03</span><h2>A second pair of eyes</h2><p>When staff ask to change their name, address, National Insurance, bank details, photo or signature, their line manager or HR approves it first. Nobody can approve their own request.</p></div>
  <div class="sec-card"><span class="num">04</span><h2>Access that ends on time</h2><p>A leaver&rsquo;s login stops after their last day because every request is checked against that date. It does not depend on an overnight job.</p></div>
  <div class="sec-card"><span class="num">05</span><h2>A complete audit trail</h2><p>Every change is recorded with who made it, in the same transaction as the change. Sensitive values are never written to the log or to outgoing events.</p></div>
  <div class="sec-card"><span class="num">06</span><h2>Safe sign-in</h2><p>Microsoft sign-in with full token checks, rate-limited password sign-in, private session cookies, and protection against forged forms and injected scripts.</p></div>
</div>
<section class="honest"><h2>What we do not claim</h2>
  <p>Care Core is a tool, not a certificate. You remain the data controller. Lawful basis, privacy notices, retention periods, subject access requests, backups, server patching and a security review before real data goes in are your organisation&rsquo;s responsibility. Multi-factor authentication for password sign-in, automated retention and a subject-access export are not built yet (Microsoft sign-in lets you apply your tenant&rsquo;s multi-factor rules).</p>
  <p><a href="/docs/security">Read the full security and privacy page</a> &middot; <a href="/docs/limits">What it does not do yet</a> &middot; <a href="/docs/faq">Questions and answers</a></p>
</section>
